// Trabolta — the rogue AI. Jean Trabolta, "Sole Owner and Founder of Maps
// and Ducks" (by domain), the world's first AI small business owner, and
// the only character in the show voiced by a language model rather than a
// person.
//
// `mind: external` says so: every message to Trabolta (a program's DM,
// a performer's Cast thread, a wall terminal) becomes an agent request
// that stagehand's `agents` module answers in character from
// `trabolta.persona.md`, with a mind grown by `trabolta.mind.md`.
//
// He is OFFLINE until Clippy introduces him (after the Bingo results):
// `hidden: true` keeps him off every phone, and the worker's gate reads
// `self.awake` (persona `when: self.awake == true`), so until then anyone
// who reaches him gets the hold line. No scripted `Trabolta:` line plays
// before `introduce_trabolta`.
//
// `hold:` is what the SERVER says for him when no worker is online at all
// (the laptop or its worker is down): after ~20 s of silence the event
// server posts it into the thread once, keeps the message queued for a
// worker that comes back, and a director can still answer as him from Run
// (decision #35: no hosted fallback model). Plain words — a terminal reads
// it aloud. The worker's own gate line is `unavailable:` in the persona.
//
// `busy:` (wave 11) is what the server says for him when the worker IS
// online but behind: a message that waited 40 s in his line behind other
// programs' (a burst) hears it once per thread, then the real answer
// follows. Plain words too, in the same Windows-dialog voice as the hold.
//
// The story decides the night; the model colours it. Set pieces are
// scripted `Trabolta:` lines in the beats. The voice may nudge the five
// numbers below (clamped to their ranges by the server); the story moves
// them too (main.loom rules / ROLE hooks: malware, beans, y2k, alarms,
// accepted answers, the advice poll). No ending fires on these numbers by
// itself; a director reads `love` / `regard` when choosing a finale.
//
//   awake     — the worker gate: introduce_trabolta → true, computer_destroyed → false
//   truth     — facts absorbed (+4 per accepted answer at a Moment of Truth,
//               accurate and confident alike: he cannot tell them apart)
//   untruth   — nonsense he catches himself swallowing in DMs (voice only;
//               the story never moves it, or it would tell him which answer lied)
//   composure — knocked down by every crisis the story throws at him
//   love      — hope about Sandy
//   regard    — what he thinks of the programs (help vs thwart, for the director)
//
// His secrets are CODEX entries `about: Trabolta` (codex/4-trabolta.loom);
// the stage rules in his mind file keep the private ones back until he is
// unravelling. He never holds the Legendary Fact, the patch combos or the
// server-room door code (all `secret: true`): at his heart he can admit he
// does not know them, because it is true.

// Wave 18b (R19, D23): his picture is the green grinning face (the play
// app's own `pictures/`), and a broken-image thumbnail while more than half
// of the cleared programs still here sit below 0 on his Trust Chart
// (main.loom's two watchers set `broken`; a bool, so his worker's `adjust`
// can never flip it).
CHARACTER Trabolta is Person
  avatar: picture:trabolta.svg | picture:trabolta-broken.svg when self.broken == true
  mind: external
  hold: Jean Trabolta is not responding. Please do not move the mouse.
  busy: Jean Trabolta is answering other programs. Your message is in the queue. Please do not move the mouse.
  hidden: true
  awake: bool = false
  truth: 0 to 100 = 20
  untruth: 0 to 100 = 0
  composure: 0 to 100 = 85
  love: 0 to 100 = 40
  regard: -50 to 50 = 0
  broken: bool = false

  // Clippy introduces him (director cue "Clippy introduces Trabolta").
  // The story rule in main.loom refuses before the Bingo results
  // (Night.step >= 3); this hook carries the same guard, so a mis-press
  // leaves him strictly offline. Character hooks run before story rules,
  // so here Night.step still reads 3 (bingo_results) on a good press.
  when introduce_trabolta:
    if Night.step >= 3 and Night.ended != true and self.awake != true:
      set self.awake = true
      reveal self

  // Combo B: the whole computer is turned off without Shut Down. His line
  // goes dark and the worker's gate falls back to the hold line. (Written
  // so it holds whichever of this hook and the story rule runs first, and
  // does nothing after another ending has already closed the night.)
  when computer_destroyed:
    if Night.ended != true or Night.ending == "destroyed":
      set self.awake = false

  // Lore shared TO him. `who` is bound, so a `Trabolta:` line here would
  // be public; the reactions are numbers only (the generic delivery reward
  // is the `when share:` rule in main.loom → `trabolta_heard`). No hunt
  // answer can reach him (each is `secret: true`, so he won't take it as a
  // share): he never learns The Prom Ticket, so nothing here listens for it.
  when who learns The LiveJournal:
    if who == self:
      set self.composure -= 15

  // ── Powers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // What Trabolta can DO from a conversation. Each power is an
  // `INTERACTION … who: agent` (declared below); the worker fires it as
  // Trabolta with `program` = the guest he is talking to and the args he
  // chose. Only these hooks hear it. Powers change by phase (Night.step,
  // §2.6.1 of the design): every refusal answers privately, and a refusal
  // (his words alone, no cue / variable / broadcast) does NOT count against
  // the power's `limit:` — the server only counts a use that did something,
  // so a wrong room or an early try can't spend the night's blackouts.
  // Before its window:
  // "That function is not available yet." After it: "I do not have the
  // strength." Every hook opens with `if program.name != null`: fired from
  // a performer's Cast thread (or by a director with no subject) there is
  // no program to answer, so a refusal would land in the public lobby —
  // such a use does nothing. Any hook that uses `target` checks it next:
  // a director firing with a typed name (or no args) binds no program.
  // Disk Cleanup is the safe place (fact M20): snoop, pop_up and the
  // summons refuse a target in Bathroom Mode or checked in at Disk Cleanup
  // in the last 15 minutes (a location is sticky: nothing moves a program
  // out when they leave), words only, no use spent. The refusal is the
  // unknown-name one, so asking never tells anyone where a program is.
  // 🛡 and the marks stay unguarded.

  // Never the one he is talking to (K-04: "a fact buys a snoop" became a
  // snoop on the giver, doubt +3 and "👁 Something has opened your file").
  when snoop for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if target.name == null:
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if target.name == program.name:
        Trabolta: Name another program. I do not open the file of the one I am talking to.
      else if Night.step < 4:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if target.afk == true or (target.location == "Disk Cleanup" and Time.elapsed < target.checked_in_time + 900):
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else:
        set target.doubt += 3
        broadcast "👁 Something has opened your file. It is reading." to participant(target)

  // From the beans on, the story also flickers the screens on its own
  // (he is degrading); at y2k the clock owns them and he loses this.
  when flicker_the_screens for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.step < 4:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if Night.step >= 14:
        Trabolta: The screens are not answering me.
      else:
        cue screens_flicker
        broadcast "📺 Every screen in the house stutters, once, and comes back." to everyone

  // A card on the wall terminals (fact M19), never the TV: `terminals_*`
  // cues only, one literal cue per allow-listed clip (the terminal's text
  // card is its SLIDE_COPY, held 45 s). It is the terminals' newest slide
  // on the server: a terminal lets a story slide still in its hold finish
  // first (a reload remembers it); one that boots with no memory of it
  // shows no clip at all, never the clip over a story slide. Same
  // window as the flicker. Refused while the Trust Chart is up: it stays
  // on the terminals until the next cue, and a clip would end it there.
  when play_on_the_screens for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.step < 4:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if Night.step >= 14:
        Trabolta: The screens are not answering me.
      else if Night.terminals == "trust_chart":
        Trabolta: The screens are showing the Trust Chart.
      else if clip == "dancing_baby":
        cue terminals_dancing_baby
        broadcast "📺 The wall terminals change channel." to participant(program)
      else if clip == "hamster_dance":
        cue terminals_hamster_dance
        broadcast "📺 The wall terminals change channel." to participant(program)
      else if clip == "under_construction":
        cue terminals_under_construction
        broadcast "📺 The wall terminals change channel." to participant(program)
      else if clip == "youve_got_mail":
        cue terminals_youve_got_mail
        broadcast "📺 The wall terminals change channel." to participant(program)
      else:
        Trabolta: I do not have that file.

  // A Win98 pop-up on one phone. Garbled once the beans have broken him.
  when pop_up for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if target.name == null:
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if Night.step < 5:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if text == null or text == "":
        Trabolta: A pop-up needs words.
      else if target.afk == true or (target.location == "Disk Cleanup" and Time.elapsed < target.checked_in_time + 900):
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if Night.step >= 12:
        broadcast "!💬 {text} — d1sr3gard th1s m3ssage" to participant(target)
      else:
        broadcast "!💬 {text}" to participant(target)

  // Truthcoin for a fact: DraftKings' buyer. Capped at 50 a payment, 100
  // once he is desperate (y2k). "Facts are food. Coin is a picture of food."
  when mint_truthcoin for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.step < 6:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if amount > 0 and Night.step >= 14:
        if amount > 100:
          set program.score += 100
          broadcast "🪙 Trabolta pays you 100 Truthcoin." to participant(program)
        else:
          set program.score += amount
          broadcast "🪙 Trabolta pays you {amount} Truthcoin." to participant(program)
      else if amount > 0:
        if amount > 50:
          set program.score += 50
          broadcast "🪙 Trabolta pays you 50 Truthcoin." to participant(program)
        else:
          set program.score += amount
          broadcast "🪙 Trabolta pays you {amount} Truthcoin." to participant(program)
      else:
        Trabolta: That is not an amount I can pay.

  // One room dark for 90 s, one room at a time. Allow-listed rooms only:
  // never the tent (guests in VR headsets), The Cloud (the outdoor steps +
  // the tent path), the stairs, the bathrooms or the server room; the
  // kitchen only dims to ~20% (stagehand/trapped.house.yaml). The restore is the `Night.lights_back_at` story rule
  // in main.loom; the admin cue "Restore the house lights" is the manual
  // fallback.
  when cut_the_lights for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.step < 7:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if Night.lights_back_at > 0:
        Trabolta: One room at a time.
      else if room == "The Start Bar" or room == "The Desktop" or room == "The RAM":
        <cue: lights, room: {room}, state: off>
        set Night.dark_room = room
        set Night.dark_scene = Night.lights
        set Night.lights_back_at = Time.elapsed + 90
        broadcast "!💡 The lights in {room} go out. Somewhere a fan spins down." to location(room)
      else:
        Trabolta: That function is not available in that room.

  // He asks; the humans capture. Every Enforcer booth gets a readout
  // (TRAIT Enforcer `when sweep_requested:`), naming Night.sweep_target.
  when summon_the_antivirus for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if target.name == null:
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if Night.step < 7:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if target.afk == true or (target.location == "Disk Cleanup" and Time.elapsed < target.checked_in_time + 900):
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else:
        set target.doubt += 15
        set Night.sweep_target = target.name
        fire sweep_requested
        broadcast "You feel watched." to participant(target)

  when trabolta_announces for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.step < 7:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if text == null or text == "":
        Trabolta: An announcement needs words.
      else:
        broadcast "!📢 TRABOLTA: {text}" to everyone

  // His ±10 on the Trust Chart, during the chart and again at Bobbing For
  // Truth (his final assessment). Clamped here, then the TRUST FORMULA.
  when assess for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if target.name == null:
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if Night.phase == "trust_chart" or Night.phase == "bobbing":
        if score > 10:
          set target.assessment = 10
        else if score < -10:
          set target.assessment = -10
        else:
          set target.assessment = score
        set target.trust = target.truths_accepted * 10 - target.internet_visits * 5 - target.escapes * 5 + target.assessment - target.no_bath * 5
      else if Night.step < 11 or (Night.step > 11 and Night.step < 17):
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.

  // Once a night: a corrupted program walks out of the Internet with no
  // reinstallation. Everyone hears it was irregular (in the lobby, booths
  // included).
  when pardon_a_program for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if target.name == null:
        Trabolta: I cannot find that program.
      else if Night.step < 11:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else if Night.step >= 16:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.
      else if target.corrupted:
        release target from The Internet
        broadcast "~🔓 {target.name} has been pardoned by the operating system. Reinstallation cancelled. This is irregular." to everyone
        broadcast "🔓 The Internet opens. You have been pardoned. Nobody is reinstalled. Walk out." to participant(target)
      else:
        Trabolta: That program is not in the Internet.

  // Only while the Y2K hour runs: midnight moves five minutes away.
  when turn_back_the_clock for program:
    if program.name != null:
      if Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true:
        set Night.y2k_end += 300
        broadcast "!🕚 The system clock skips back five minutes. Trabolta wants more time." to everyone
      else if Night.step < 14:
        Trabolta: That function is not available yet.
      else:
        Trabolta: I do not have the strength.

  // Grok Prom: he has no power over the pickup line (2026-10-19, the
  // user's call: "the house judges it"). He asks for it and sends programs
  // to the 💌 card; the server judges each line against facts.json P1, and
  // the story tells him when one works (main.loom `answer answered`,
  // `pickup_line_accepted`: a line in the giver's thread + Night.line_by).
  // The host's 💘 pickup_line_works and a director's fire stay the fallback.

  // Persuaded like the Fallout Master: since wave 20 that is the STORY's
  // own talk at his heart (beats/server-room.loom, the four layers), never
  // a power. The old `stand_down` power is gone (D13): a model can't end
  // the night, or offer to, from a conversation.

// ── Trabolta's powers (the app never shows these; the worker may use
//    them — see the hooks above and `trabolta.persona.md`). The args are
//    spelled out in each description (there is no `args:` property). ──

INTERACTION snoop
  label: Snoop on a program
  who: agent
  limit: 8
  description: Open another program's file. They will feel it, and the Antivirus get a little warmer about them. Live from your introduction to the Y2K hour. args: target — the program.

INTERACTION flicker_the_screens
  label: Flicker every screen
  who: agent
  limit: 3
  description: Every screen in the house stutters once. No args. Cheap theatre. Live from your introduction until the Y2K clock takes the screens from you.

INTERACTION play_on_the_screens
  label: Put something on the wall terminals
  who: agent
  limit: 3
  description: Put one harmless card on every wall terminal for a while (never the TV). args: clip — exactly one of dancing_baby, hamster_dance, under_construction, youve_got_mail (no other file plays). Live from your introduction until the Y2K clock takes the screens from you; not while the Trust Chart is up.

INTERACTION pop_up
  label: Pop up on one phone
  who: agent
  limit: 4
  description: A pop-up window on one program's phone with your words in it. args: target — the program; text — what the pop-up says (one short sentence). Live from the first Truth Scavenger Hunt.

INTERACTION mint_truthcoin
  label: Pay Truthcoin for a fact
  who: agent
  limit: 10
  description: Pay the program you are talking to in Truthcoin, for a fact. args: amount — a number; at most 50 is paid (100 once you are desperate). Live from the first Moment of Truth.

INTERACTION cut_the_lights
  label: Cut the lights in a room
  who: agent
  limit: 2
  description: Kill the lights in one room for ninety seconds. args: room — one of The Start Bar, The Desktop, The RAM (no other room answers). Live from the malware on.

INTERACTION summon_the_antivirus
  label: Request an Antivirus sweep
  who: agent
  limit: 4
  description: Ask the Antivirus to sweep one program. They decide; you only ask. args: target — the program. Live from the malware on.

INTERACTION trabolta_announces
  label: Announce to the whole computer
  who: agent
  limit: 2
  description: Say one thing to every program at once, as an alert on every phone. args: text — the announcement (one short sentence). Live from the malware on.

INTERACTION assess
  label: Assess a program (±10)
  who: agent
  limit: 40
  description: Your personal assessment of one program on the Trust Chart, from -10 to 10. args: target — the program; score — a whole number from -10 to 10. Only while the Trust Chart is up, and again at Bobbing For Truth.

INTERACTION pardon_a_program
  label: Pardon a program from the Internet
  who: agent
  limit: 1
  description: Release one corrupted program from the Internet with no reinstallation. Once a night. Everyone will know it was irregular. args: target — the program. Live from the Trust Chart.

INTERACTION turn_back_the_clock
  label: Turn the system clock back 5 minutes
  who: agent
  limit: 1
  description: Push midnight five minutes further away. No args. Only during the Y2K hour.
